From 0989963c688fd3a0eb9427bf5bfc297e58ac5a47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vitaly Lipatov <lav@etersoft.ru>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:41:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 29/70] drm/msm/adreno: consume validated TCL ACPI GPU and GMU
 resources

The OEM composite GPU device must be represented as separate Adreno and
GMU consumers. These drivers need explicit resource, supplier and
firmware-node references rather than OF-only matching.

Add the guarded TCL platform path with chip, memory-window and
zap-shader reservation checks. Resolve the GMU and power relationships
through firmware references and integrate the ACPI resource path with
Adreno initialization. The board coordinator, IORT mapping and
clock/domain providers are separate prerequisites. This targets native
GPU rendering and does not implement hardware video decoding.
---
